# Riverpod Patterns

## State Class (Freezed)

```dart
@freezed
abstract class UserState with _$UserState {
  const factory UserState({
    @Default(false) bool isLoading,
    @Default(null) User? user,
    @Default(null) String? error,
  }) = _UserState;
}
```

## Controller (Riverpod Codegen)

```dart
@riverpod
class UserController extends _$UserController {
  @override
  FutureOr<UserState> build() async => const UserState();

  Future<void> fetchUser() async {
    state = const AsyncLoading();
    try {
      final user = await ref.read(userRepositoryProvider).fetchUser();
      state = AsyncData(UserState(user: user));
    } catch (e, stack) {
      state = AsyncError(e, stack);
    }
  }
}
```

## State Access

- `ref.watch()` - Reactive state (rebuilds on change)
- `ref.read()` - One-time access (in callbacks)
- `ref.listen()` - Side effects (snackbars, navigation)

## AsyncValue

Use AsyncValue for async operations: AsyncData, AsyncLoading, AsyncError.
